  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 6509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We take it for granted that our universe\ncontains planets, stars and galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6509,
    "dDurationMs": 4231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because those are the things we see but\nthe only reason these big structures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10740,
    "dDurationMs": 5459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exist is because of the nature of\nnothingness - empty space. But to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16199,
    "dDurationMs": 4201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understand why we have to go back to the\nbeginning. The very beginning. The big bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, I always thought that in\nthe Big Bang the observable universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24720,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "started as a point and then just\nexpanded steadily more or less to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28650,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "point that we're at today but that's not\nactually how it happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32830,
    "dDurationMs": 5569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were four different phases in the universe's\nexpansion. To start it was expanding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38399,
    "dDurationMs": 5371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "steadily but then after just a tiny\nfraction of a second the expansion just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43770,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blew up and the whole universe increased\nin size by like ten to the twenty six"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48870,
    "dDurationMs": 5790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times in a very short period of time and\nthat period is known as inflation and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54660,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then just as abruptly as it began\ninflation stopped and after that the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59640,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe continued expanding but at a\ndecreasing rate so the expansion of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64650,
    "dDurationMs": 4829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe was actually slowing down which\nis exactly what you expect if the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69479,
    "dDurationMs": 3631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe is full of massive objects that\ngravitationally attract each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73110,
    "dDurationMs": 3899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then about five or six billion years\nago the expansion of the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77009,
    "dDurationMs": 5031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "started speeding up again and this is\nthought to be caused by dark energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82040,
    "dDurationMs": 6219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an energy tied to space. So before that time\nthere was enough matter, the matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88259,
    "dDurationMs": 3811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "density was high enough, that it was\npulling everything back together slowing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92070,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down the expansion but once the universe\nreached a critical size"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96360,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then there was enough dark energy\nto start pushing things apart and that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101040,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the phase that we're still in the\nexpansion of the universe is accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this story doesn't\nreally explain the formation of galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109170,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until you tie in the nature of\nnothingness"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112860,
    "dDurationMs": 4829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now ordinarily we think of everything\naround us as made of particles of atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117689,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and electrons but our best theories of\nphysics are actually field theories that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122009,
    "dDurationMs": 5551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say all these particles should be seen\nas just excitations in fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127560,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The word \"field\" always gets me because it makes me\nthink of... well, fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131720,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a field is just something that has\na value everywhere in space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137060,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So every subatomic particle has its own field: an\nelectron field, an up quark field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142220,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a down quark field, a neutrino field, and so on..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144820,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And anywhere there's an excitation in this field"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147100,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is some energy in the\nfield"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149360,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well that is where we will observe\nparticles. So out in completely empty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154520,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space where the values for all of these\nfields are basically zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159960,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but here's the thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161060,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's impossible to make a field\nperfectly flat and 0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166280,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You cannot take a quantum field and make it completely quiet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170500,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the Heisenberg uncertainty principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172380,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It says you can't take a particle\nand pinpoint it to exactly zero energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176440,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "likewise you can't take a quantum field\nand make it exactly flat everywhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181420,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this is important because ordinarily\nthese fluctuations are really really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185150,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tiny and they only affect subatomic\nprocesses but during that period of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190220,
    "dDurationMs": 7140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inflation the universe expanded in size\nso rapidly and so incredibly that those"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197360,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tiny fluctuations got blown up to the\nscale of the observable universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203180,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, without them we think the matter\ndistribution in the universe would have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206840,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been completely homogeneous completely\nuniform and that means the gravitational"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211700,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "force on any object in the universe\nwould have been the same in all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214970,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "directions which means nothing would\never have collapsed into the big"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219530,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "structures that we see today but thanks\nto these fluctuations there were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223549,
    "dDurationMs": 4261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slightly denser and less dense regions\nand of course the denser regions had"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227810,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stronger gravitational fields so they\npulled in the matter from around them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231950,
    "dDurationMs": 4319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that clumped together the matter into\nhuge gas clouds that would go on to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236269,
    "dDurationMs": 4411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the galaxies that contain the stars and\nthe planets and the things we know today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240680,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can actually see the imprint of\nthese quantum fluctuations in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245239,
    "dDurationMs": 3601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leftover radiation from the Big Bang the\ncosmic microwave background radiation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248840,
    "dDurationMs": 6630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the quantum fluctuations in the fields\nwere amplified to big classical fluctuations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255470,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the density of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256590,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "matter from place to place and those\nfluctuations in the density of matter show up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260940,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the universe today as temperature\ndifferences in the cosmic background"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264510,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "radiation and ultimately in things like\nstars and planets and galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268950,
    "dDurationMs": 6990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it is incredible that without these\nfluctuations in the vacuum these tiny"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275940,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "insignificant things that we take for\ngranted our universe might really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280410,
    "dDurationMs": 6580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "contain nothing. Nothing of interest\nanyway..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287010,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Speaking of vacuum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288650,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this episode was supported in part by Dyson\nwho sent me their 360 eye vacuuming robot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294030,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's got this little camera on the top\nthat can see 360 degrees around it now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298830,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it uses that vision plus some complex\nmath and trigonometry to work out its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303780,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "location precisely and to figure out\nwhere it's cleaned already and where it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307260,
    "dDurationMs": 4409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still needs to clean it actually makes a\nmap that you can see on your phone using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311669,
    "dDurationMs": 4441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the dyson app and you can use that app\nalso to control the vacuum or to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316110,
    "dDurationMs": 4529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "schedule it even when you're not at home\nso I for one welcome robots taking over"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320639,
    "dDurationMs": 2671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the housework you want to find out more\nyou can click the link in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323310,
    "dDurationMs": 3479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "description so i want to thank Dyson for\nsupporting me and I want to thank my"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326789,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "patreon supporters and of course you for\nwatching"
    } ]
  } ]
}
